<TextPage lang="en" title="About" altUrl="/es/acerca/">
  <p>
    Goat Science is a science communication blog about goats. Every week it publishes a summary of one recent or
    particularly interesting scientific paper, explained in plain language and always with the full reference to the
    original work.
  </p>
  <p>Every summary answers the same questions, so you always know where to look:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>What did the authors ask?</li>
    <li>What did they do?</li>
    <li>What did they find?</li>
    <li>Why does it matter?</li>
    <li>What are the study's limitations?</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Who writes it</h2>
  <p>
    Anastasio Argüello, Professor of Animal Production at the University of Las Palmas de Gran Canaria. His research
    focuses on goat science: colostrum biology, passive immunity transfer, meat and milk quality, and neonatal ruminant
    physiology.
  </p>
  <p>ORCID: <a href="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4426-0678">0000-0002-4426-0678</a></p>
</TextPage>
